intent: >
  Remove 18 fabricated client testimonials from 6 service pages and
  replace each with a 'Steve's Approach to <Service>' principles section
  that's honest (Steve's voice, not invented clients).

slice: "?/?"
kind: fix
behavior_change: additive

reversibility: trivial

scope:
  declared: []
  actual:
    - src/hardscaping.njk
    - src/landscape-lighting.njk
    - src/irrigation-systems.njk
    - src/vegetable-gardens.njk
    - src/plant-selection.njk
    - src/garden-consultation.njk
  drift: []

proof:
  tests_run: "Manual: Eleventy dev server rebuild on each file save (clean, no errors), Chrome verification on /hardscaping/ confirmed new headings render and zero blockquotes / zero fake names in served HTML"
  result: green
  failing: 0

tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    Static template content replacement. No logic. Verified by build
    output (Eleventy wrote 35 files cleanly on each save) and DOM
    inspection on one representative page.

assumptions:
  - "All 6 testimonial blocks are placeholders, not real clients (corroborated by the same Sarah/Michael/Sarah pattern repeated across pages with different feedback — no real client said all those things)"
  - "Steve will eventually replace the principles copy with his actual voice; current text is best-guess of how he'd describe his approach"
  - "Real testimonials can be added later as a separate section without disrupting the principles block"

specifications:
  - "Service pages display author-voiced design principles instead of client-voiced testimonials when real testimonials aren't available"
  - "Principles section uses the same shape as newport-beach.njk (bg-gray-50 card on bg-white section, or bg-white card on bg-gray-50 section, depending on existing bg alternation)"
  - "Section heading pattern: 'Steve's Approach to <Service>' (consultation page uses 'What to Expect from a Consultation' because that page is itself the consultation, not a service)"

deviations_from_plan: >
  No plan file for this slice — ad-hoc cleanup work in response to user
  asking 'clean up the testimonials on the other service pages'. Followed
  the established pattern from the in-flight PR #8 newport-beach
  principles section.

addresses: []

trade_offs: >
  Could have left these as a 'real testimonials wanted' TODO, but the
  invented quotes are deceitful in the meantime. Better to ship honest
  principles content now and add real testimonials when available than to
  leave fakery live. Also: scoping this as a separate PR off master keeps
  PR #8 reviewable as-is.

interfaces: {}

self_review:
  consistency: >
    All 6 sections use the same markup pattern as newport-beach.njk's
    'How Steve Designs for Newport Beach' section. Card bg alternates
    to match each page's existing section bg-color (preserves visual
    alternation in the layout).
  honesty: >
    Removes the core deceit pattern (invented quotes attributed to fake
    clients). Principles copy is best-guess Steve voice — flagged for
    Steve to rewrite when convenient, but the worst-case outcome here
    (Steve's voice approximated) is far better than the prior state
    (Lisa M. claiming Steve designed her favorite spot).
  pre_existing_debt: >
    These were invented in the original site build, not by this session.
    Cleanup is bounded to the testimonial blocks. Other pages (homepage
    testimonials at index.njk, homepage 'Testimonials Modal') NOT
    touched — different context, separate decision.

confidence: high
reviewer_attention:
  - "All 6 files: skim Steve's principle copy and rewrite anything that doesn't sound like him. The voice approximation is the weakest link in this PR"
